[Music]  my name is eris i am the co-owner of all  together leather and i have been a  professional leather worker for five  years altogether leather is canada's  first queer owned cobbling shop today  i'm going to walk you through how are  your store a faded and poorly re-dyed  your handbag this is our client's  handbag she brought it in because she  had previously tried to re-dye it at a  different shop that did not strip the  dye properly when you look at this bag  you can see that it is gray the handles  are poorly warped and chipped  [Music]  this dior bag is leaking dye and so we  are going to have to deglaze it to start  we will need to prep this bag by taping  off all portions that we do not want to  get dye on to strip the bag we will  start by putting on our safety equipment  deglazer is a very strong chemical that  is formulated to remove sealant coats  and previous dye layers from leather  we will deglaze the bag by going in  small circles with a medium rough sponge  to get the previous dye off in the  previous ceiling coat off  we need to evenly distribute the  deglazer over the bag to ensure that the  dye will evenly go back into the bag  after the fact  we're using a professional oil tan dye  formulated for leather it is better than  alcohol-based dyes as it gives a more  even coverage  we will be using a paint brush for all  of the quilted areas to make sure we get  the creases and wool dauber for the  bottom where it is even leather  we are using a large flat crystals  paintbrush to make sure that our strokes  are wide and even making for a uniform  color  interiors of bags pose challenges  because you are not able to dye liners  and so you have to make sure that you  don't hit the liner which is why we  protect it with tape  the handle's edges are too badly cracked  to be restored and the handles  themselves are bleeding so much dye that  we do not think we can successfully  prevent dye complaining out of them in  the future we are going to remake 